  "instructions": [
    "In a small bowl, combine yeast, warm milk, and 1 tsp sugar. Let it sit for 5 min to activate.",
    "In a separate bowl, mix together flour, salt, and pepper.",
    "Melt butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onion, carrot, and celery, and cook until the vegetables are soft.",
    "Add garlic and cook for 1 min more.",
    "Add boudin-noir and cook, breaking it apart with a spoon, until lightly browned.",
    "Add flour mixture and cook for 1 min, stirring constantly.",
    "Stir in cheddar, eggs, parsley, and yeast mixture. Cook, stirring constantly, until mixture thickens.",
    "Transfer the mixture to a greased plate or tray and refrigerate for 30 min to set.",
    "Cut the mixture into 1-inch pieces and place them on a greased lazy Susan spinner.",
    "Cook in a preheated oven at 375°F for 18-20 min, or until golden brown on top and crispy on the bottom.",
    "Serve warm and enjoy!"
  ],
